<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3238" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμ-αῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			Aeol.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκμαος</span></b>  Jo. Gramm.<i><span class="en">
			<u>Comp.</u>
			2.14
		</span></i>; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>in full bloom, at
				prime, vigorous</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῶλοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					405
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥβη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμαῖος φύσιν</span>
			<i>in the prime of</i> strength, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				441
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τὸν ὀργήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Tim.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλλει ἀκμαία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					127
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀκμαιότατον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					5.22
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμαίων λέσχη</span> at Chalcis, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.298d
			</span></i>:—
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πρὸς ἔρωτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.221
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DDeor.</u>
				8.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				15.10
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμαίως, ἔχειν κατὰ τὴν ἡλικίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					31.29.7
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ότερον</span>
			<i>more vigorously</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				4.525
			</span></i>:—of things, <i>at the height</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἀκμαιότατος καιρὸς τῆς ἡμέρας</span>,
			i. e. noon, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.102.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀ. τοῦ χειμῶνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>An.</u>
					4.7.1
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Rhet.,
				<i>belonging to the supreme effort, culmination of
			oratory</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔννοιαι, λόγος</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Id.</u>
				1.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Inv.</u>
				4.4
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Id.</u>
				1.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>in time, in season</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καιρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PTeb.</u>
					24.56
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>, 
				Sup.
			); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἡμέραι</span> the
				<i>seasonable</i> days, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				5.180c
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				10.2
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antip.Sid.
			</span></i>): neut. pl. as Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμαἶ᾽ ἂν μόλοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					921
				</span></i>
			 (cj.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
